{
  "@context": "../../context.jsonld",
  "@type": "Capability",
  "critical": false,
  "description": "Hybrid rocket engine design and manufacturing: solid fuel grain (HTPB, paraffin wax, or cross-linked polymer) paired with a liquid or gaseous oxidizer (N2O, LOX, GOX) fed through a pressure-fed or pump-fed system. Combines the storability and simplicity of solids with the throttleability, stop/restart capability, and safety (non-detonable, segregated fuel and oxidizer) of liquids. Delivers 250-350 s vacuum Isp with regression rates of 0.5-2.0 mm/s, enabling crewed suborbital flight (SpaceShipOne/Two), sounding rockets, and upper stages.",
